From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ViewRootImpl: knob LEFT/RIGHT as focus order with a property

The Car Thing has one rotary knob, which sends DPAD_LEFT and DPAD_RIGHT. With
directional focus search, a knob cannot reach every view: in a list, LEFT and
RIGHT find nothing, and in two columns up/down orders depend on the direction.
With ro.config.knob_sequential_focus=true, a LEFT or RIGHT key that the app
does not handle moves the focus as SHIFT+TAB and TAB do (FOCUS_BACKWARD,
FOCUS_FORWARD). Apps that handle the keys in dispatchKeyEvent (DiPlay's CarPlay
screen, CptHome) do not change. Without the property, nothing changes.

---
--- a/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java
@@ -165,6 +165,15 @@
             "ro.emu.win_outset_bottom_px";
 
     /**
+     * PlayThing: the device has one rotary knob, which sends DPAD_LEFT and DPAD_RIGHT. With
+     * this property, a LEFT or RIGHT key that the app does not handle moves the focus to the
+     * previous or next view in focus order (as SHIFT+TAB and TAB), so the knob reaches every
+     * focusable view. Apps that handle the keys themselves do not change.
+     */
+    private static final boolean KNOB_SEQUENTIAL_FOCUS =
+            SystemProperties.getBoolean("ro.config.knob_sequential_focus", false);
+
+    /**
      * Maximum time we allow the user to roll the trackball enough to generate
      * a key event, before resetting the counters.
      */
@@ -4930,12 +4939,12 @@
             switch (event.getKeyCode()) {
                 case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_DPAD_LEFT:
                     if (event.hasNoModifiers()) {
-                        direction = View.FOCUS_LEFT;
+                        direction = KNOB_SEQUENTIAL_FOCUS ? View.FOCUS_BACKWARD : View.FOCUS_LEFT;
                     }
                     break;
                 case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_DPAD_RIGHT:
                     if (event.hasNoModifiers()) {
-                        direction = View.FOCUS_RIGHT;
+                        direction = KNOB_SEQUENTIAL_FOCUS ? View.FOCUS_FORWARD : View.FOCUS_RIGHT;
                     }
                     break;
                 case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_DPAD_UP:
